# ── Chapter 24 fidelity pins: "Findings About People" ───────────────────────────
#
# FS-CVF-003 executable coverage is delegated to book-1/source/state-form.pins.nibli.
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   ./verify.sh --only book-1/24-findings-about-people.pins.nibli
#   ./verify.sh          # all substantive pins and contradiction checks

# WHAT FALSE MEANS HERE — three kinds, and only one is a verdict. A FALSE on a
# corpus name this KB never mentions is real but empty: nothing could have made
# it TRUE. A non-corpus name is not a FALSE at all — the run aborts, pins not
# trustworthy. And a well-formed query on an argument its relation never
# carries is a vacuous green that passes forever. Article 0a closes the
# ASSERTION side only — a widening fact aborts the run rather than loading —
# but a QUERY on an unmentioned name still answers a clean FALSE, so kind one
# remains. Pin a FALSE only where the KB could have said TRUE, and say in
# the comment what would flip it.

:expect-pins 177

# The file runs the chapter's three strands in the order their state allows:
# who holds the authority to sign, then the limits of a finding, then the
# paired finding and its reach, whose closing weaker-rule control is an
# unscoped acceptance and must come last.

# ── Who holds the authority to sign ───────────────────────────────────────────

# "Each route needs a seating, no recall, and a positive record of clear
# history, witnessed in an earlier version of the record and kept in the
# version in force." And "A restriction recorded in an earlier version and
# kept in the version in force withholds the authority."

# Voss's custody case, for the relief tests further down: "Custody needs its
# own positive merits, defence, procedure, current authority and lawful
# placement evidence." These entries supply the merits, a severity finding,
# the placement and intake; the case-bound review comes with Voss below.
